From dedb12ec4b5a1c80b0bf75dafa6d512eedaa58dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HibernalGlow <3090253564@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:38:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: boot the workbench payload a build ships

The packaged profile only ever carried upstream bundles, so the shipped app showed upstream chrome no matter what the checkout composed. A build can now hand in a payload directory: the pack stage copies it to Resources/xaihi, and a freshly created profile gains its bundles as file: copies plus the xaihi-core patch row that points the workbench route at the shipped document. Unset keeps the resource list and the profile byte-identical to upstream, which the specs pin in both directions.
